#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""wb-instructions -- make the user's rules/roles/skills available to EVERY harness, not just
Claude Code (SPEC-V3-MODELS.md section E).

  wb-instructions sync [--dry-run] [--harness <id>] [--force]

Canonical sources (never written by this tool, only read):
  ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md
  ~/.claude/roles/orchestrator.md
  ~/.claude/roles/agent.md
  ~/.claude/skills/*/SKILL.md

For every non-Claude harness these three files get concatenated into ONE generated
instructions file (each such CLI only auto-reads a single file -- no separate system-prompt
slot, no native skill feature), with a small, table-driven set of Claude-Code-specific
substitutions applied (see REPLACEMENTS below) and a skills index appended. Each generated
file starts with a marker block (source paths, timestamp, SHA-256 of sources AND of its own
body) so a second `sync` is a true no-op when nothing changed, and a hand-edited target is
detected (content hash mismatch) and refused rather than silently overwritten.

Separately, `sync` also drops a `<!-- wb:routing-table:start/end -->` marker pair around the
existing worker-routing table in ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md and around the matching reference line in
~/.claude/roles/orchestrator.md -- insertion only, not one other word touched -- so a future
`wb-state models table` fill-in can keep that table current without hand edits.
"""
